WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.535
- On Fresh Prince,

00:00:01.535 --> 00:00:04.350
I loved the show and I felt
like even back then it,

00:00:04.350 --> 00:00:06.680
it talked about a lot of subjects

00:00:06.680 --> 00:00:08.330
that were really important back then,

00:00:08.330 --> 00:00:11.692
but sadly, I feel like still resonate now.

00:00:11.692 --> 00:00:12.970
- Yes.
- What is that like,

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:14.440
like being a part, 'cause I know,

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.110
was it ever hard during the show?

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.060
'Cause y'all did, you brought up topics

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:18.893
that were hard topics
- Yes.

00:00:18.893 --> 00:00:20.970
- to talk about and it
was such a family show.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:22.720
- You know, we, we,

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.940
back then we used to always
laugh at it 'cause it was like

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:26.810
the very special episode of Fresh Prince.

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:27.643
- Yeah.
- Right.

00:00:27.643 --> 00:00:28.476
And, and, and you know,
- Dramatic music.

00:00:28.476 --> 00:00:29.470
- it was very dramatic.

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:30.830
It would be like something silly,

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.580
but, but we did, you
know, we, we touched on

00:00:33.580 --> 00:00:35.970
I think because of the setup of the show

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:39.910
with Will coming from West
Philadelphia, moving to Bel Air,

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:43.515
the idea of rich and
poor, black and white,

00:00:43.515 --> 00:00:45.600
black and other black, right?

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.580
Like, like how it, all
the dynamics of it all

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:51.130
and so the storylines
always seemed to work

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:53.530
because they came from real places.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:54.363
- Yeah.
- They came from

00:00:54.363 --> 00:00:58.190
real experiences that we
all had to deal with, right?

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:01.090
And so one episode where we're
pulled over by the police,

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:04.250
right and the idea that Carlton,

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:06.110
right, just was like,

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:07.410
he pulled us over because we're speeding,

00:01:07.410 --> 00:01:08.270
it's not because we're black.

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:09.940
He would, he treated us this way because,

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:11.770
because he understood right and wrong.

00:01:11.770 --> 00:01:13.620
That's all he, that's all he knew.

00:01:13.620 --> 00:01:14.700
- Yeah.
- And so you could touch

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.360
on these subjects

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:19.570
without really being preachy

00:01:19.570 --> 00:01:22.330
and really saying, this
is how it is, you know?

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:24.010
And I've heard Will say this many times,

00:01:24.010 --> 00:01:27.770
it's like, you know, police
brutality didn't just start,

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:28.870
it's just being filmed.

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:29.703
- Yeah, I was gonna say,
- You know.

00:01:29.703 --> 00:01:30.536
- I've heard people say that a lot,

00:01:30.536 --> 00:01:31.369
it's been filmed now, yeah.

00:01:31.369 --> 00:01:32.202
- It's just being filmed.
- Yeah.

00:01:32.202 --> 00:01:33.035
- That's the difference.

00:01:33.035 --> 00:01:34.090
This has always been happening.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:34.923
- Yeah.
- And so,

00:01:34.923 --> 00:01:36.030
and by the way, my dad's a cop,

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.320
my grandmother was a cop.
- Yeah.

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:39.340
- So I come from law enforcement,

00:01:39.340 --> 00:01:40.710
but there is a reality,

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:42.360
there are good cops
and there are bad cops.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.590
There are cops that do the right thing

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.100
and there are cops that
don't do the right thing,

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:46.970
just like all people,

00:01:46.970 --> 00:01:47.803
right.
- Yeah.

00:01:47.803 --> 00:01:51.050
- We are, we are in every aspect
of life, there are mirrors

00:01:51.050 --> 00:01:54.490
and we are a mirror to
every aspect of, of society

00:01:54.490 --> 00:01:57.500
and so what was wonderful
was being able to,

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:59.671
to say that and to show those stories

00:01:59.671 --> 00:02:02.250
and to have those real conversations

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.031
and a lot of those
conversations happened on set

00:02:05.031 --> 00:02:07.123
as we were getting ready
to film it, you know?

00:02:07.123 --> 00:02:08.600
- But, and a lot of those conversations

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.792
happened in people's homes
after watching the episode.

00:02:10.792 --> 00:02:12.472
- And that was the hope.
- With friends and, yeah

00:02:12.472 --> 00:02:13.410
and that's the thing,

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:15.770
anytime you can, you know,
be a form of some kind of art

00:02:15.770 --> 00:02:17.440
that, that is thought provoking

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:19.420
that makes people have those
conversations afterwards

00:02:19.420 --> 00:02:20.306
- Yeah.
- job well done.

00:02:20.306 --> 00:02:23.107
- Yeah well, it, it, it, see
that people seem to like it.

00:02:23.107 --> 00:02:23.940
- You know what,
- They, they

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:26.195
- it is kind of successful.
- it's kind of stayed around

00:02:26.195 --> 00:02:27.028
a little bit.

00:02:27.028 --> 00:02:27.861
(laughing)

00:02:27.861 --> 00:02:28.694
- Yeah, that Will Smith guy,

00:02:28.694 --> 00:02:29.930
whatever happened to him.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:31.277
- No one knows.

